# Committed on purpose, unlike .env.local — see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md#web-build-config.
#
# Next.js inlines every NEXT_PUBLIC_* var into the client JS bundle at BUILD time, and
# production builds run locally on a developer machine (there's no Cloudflare-hosted build
# step that injects these). Before this file existed, the only copy of these values lived
# in one machine's .env.local, gitignored — if that file or machine were lost, nobody else
# could rebuild a correct production bundle. This file is that backup.
#
# Every value below is safe to commit:
#   - NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL / NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID: not secrets.
#   - NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID: a public client identifier by design (same category as an
#     OAuth client ID or a Stripe publishable key) — see https://docs.privy.io.
#   - NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_RPC_URL: the public, keyless Base RPC endpoint — never apps/api's
#     own paid QuickNode URL. That paid URL briefly lived here before 2026-09-14, a real,
#     live exposure, since NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars ship straight to every browser's JS bundle.
#   - NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL: a *separate*, dedicated Helius key — deliberately not the
#     fully public api.mainnet-beta.solana.com endpoint (tried first, but too unreliable
#     for Privy's own browser-side transaction simulation/confirmation — real trades failed
#     with "error preparing your transaction"), and just as deliberately NOT the same key
#     apps/api's own SOLANA_RPC_URL uses. This key's own rate limit/quota is scoped to
#     browser traffic only; if it's ever exposed or abused, the backend's trading-critical
#     quota is completely unaffected. Never reuse apps/api's own SOLANA_RPC_URL key here —
#     see lib/solana-config.ts's own doc comment on why that's a different trust boundary.
#
#     TEMPORARY EXCEPTION (2026-09-15): the dedicated frontend key
#     (6510b4c8-2b2c-4216-928b-b34f1bf77c86) started returning "Unauthorized" — almost
#     certainly collateral damage from regenerating the *backend's* Helius key the same day
#     (some Helius account actions appear to invalidate other keys on the account). Pointed
#     at apps/api's own new key below as a stop-gap so live testing wasn't blocked. Get this
#     its own fresh dedicated key when there's a moment and swap it back in — this line is a
#     deliberate, logged exception to the rule above, not a silent reversal of it.
#
# .env.local (gitignored) still exists for local overrides and still takes precedence over
# this file per Next.js's own env-file precedence — this file is the floor everyone can
# rebuild from, not a replacement for .env.local during normal local development.

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api-production-a88d.up.railway.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=8453
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.base.org
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=cmty6tphj04q00clda1zu11hw
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=706c5d5d-f82d-4357-9cbc-fb0b7504590b
